      },
      "worked": "By the division transformation,\n$$x^3+ax+b=x(x+1)Q(x)+3x+5.$$\nSubstitute $x=0$:\n$$b=5.$$\nSubstitute $x=-1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}-1-a+b&=2\\\\-1-a+5&=2\\\\a&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $a=2$ and $b=5$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
